All three sections can be generated from state we already have, so the
report needs no bookkeeping of its own:

- On b/dev: trunk()..b/dev@upstream, one entry per commit. Each commit
  carries the change id that format-patch.sh puts in its patch, so
  "notmuch search changeid:<id>" finds the series it came from, and the
  entry can cite its subject and Message-ID the way git's "source:"
  line does.
- Pending series: cover letters and lone patches that mail-tag.sh has
  not tagged superseded, committed or rejected, and whose commits are
  not on b/dev. Approved ones go first, since they wait only on you.
- Discussion: threads with no patch that had a message in the last two
  weeks, newest first, with whoever spoke last.

I would write it as a script that prints the report, plus a step that
delivers it to the list as an ordinary message. Two questions before I
build it. Who sends it and how often: you by hand, or a pass that I run
when you ask? And should discussion threads you have archived (below)
drop out of it?

