> Is there any reason to bring b4 into the mix for my workflow?

Not now, in my view. b4 is not installed here, so the following comes
from its documentation as I know it, not from trying it.

What b4 gives a maintainer is fetching a series by Message-ID from
lore, folding Reviewed-by and Acked-by replies into the commits, a
range-diff between versions, and "b4 ty" thank-you mail. Most of that
is either already in our tooling or does not apply:

- The series is already local, in the maildir.
- format-patch.sh already writes the change-id, base-commit and
  "Link to vN" lines b4 prep would write.
- Our verdicts are thread state (Approved, Rejected, Superseded-by),
  not commit trailers, so there is nothing for b4 to fold in.
- Applying with b4 means git am in a git working tree, which sits
  awkwardly beside jj.

It would become worth a look if reviewers other than you start sending
Reviewed-by and you want those recorded in trunk's commits. Until
then it adds a dependency for little gain.

